{
  "about": [
    "The Govee models SYNQ drives (wave L2), read by scripts/gen-govee-scenes.ts into the app's and the bridge's tables.",
    "A model in catalogue.json and not listed here gets `defaults`. Fields: name and kind (from Govee's own store where it",
    "still sells the model, else the SKU); dialect, the colour sub-mode SYNQ starts with (0x15 type-tagged RGBIC, 0x0b",
    "RGBIC with a segment mask, 0x0d RGB + Kelvin, 0x02 plain RGB) and dialects, the ones the guard lets through (the",
    "lamp's own `aa 05` answer can move SYNQ to another of them); segments (0: one colour for the whole light, or a",
    "count the lamp reports in `aa 40`); kelvin; brightnessMax (100, or 254 for the app's other scale); music (the lamp's",
    "own music modes, with names); diy; proven (what the developer has seen on the lamp). Everything not proven is UNVERIFIED",
    "and listed in docs/devices/LIGHTING.md.",
    "Sources: the H6076 by the developer; H66A0, H1A42, H61F5, H617A from Fredde87/ha-govee-led-ble's COMPATIBILITY.md and",
    "COMMANDS.md (MIT); the 0x15 group with a 15-segment mask (H6053, H6072, H6102, H6199) and the 0x02 default from",
    "Beshelmek/govee_ble_lights (MIT, light.py SEGMENTED_MODELS); names from us/ca/uk/eu.govee.com product pages, and",
    "for models Govee no longer sells, from the Wayback Machine's copy of Govee's own product page (the photo pass),",
    "which also gives each its form (kind: floor-lamp, tv, bar, strip, neon, panel; the page draws the light by it).",
    "H605B, H6079, H6175 and H6176 come from those pages too: they are in no scene catalogue, so they get the defaults",
    "and follow what the lamp itself reports."
  ],
